<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kyawswa of Pagan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1260s–<a href="/years/1299">1299</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kyawswa was king of Pagan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> from 1289 to 1297. He inherited a kingdom broken by the Mongol invasions and controlled little more than the capital, while three brothers held the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyaukse">Kyaukse</a> district. In 1297 he accepted Yuan overlordship to protect himself, but the brothers overthrew him the same year and executed him in 1299.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Narathihapate’s son <b>Kyawswa</b> reigned over a reduced realm as a Yuan vassal, while real power passed to the three Shan-Burman brothers of Myinsaing, who deposed him in 1297, ending the kingdom; their successors founded Pinya and later Ava.</blockquote><a href="/empire/pagan-kingdom">Pagan Kingdom · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>King <b>Kyawswa of Pagan</b>, who held little more than the capital and had accepted Yuan overlordship to protect himself, was overthrown by the three Myinsaing brothers, nominally his viceroys.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/december-17">17 December in history</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1297 they overthrew King <b>Kyawswa of Pagan</b>, who had accepted Mongol vassalage, and took control of the Kyaukse rice granary.</blockquote><a href="/state/myinsaing-kingdom">Myinsaing Kingdom</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Bagan, in what is now <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a>. Died in Kyaukse District, in what is now <a href="/countries/myanmar">Myanmar</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=21.17,94.86&amp;year=1285" aria-label="Bagan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7100 1381 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Kyawswa of Pagan"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7550 1651h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7550 1651h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=21.17,94.86&amp;year=1285">What was here in 1285? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
